# Cards Structured Reference

This file reorganizes card knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by other deterministic knowledge sources.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/cards for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Cards
Type: System
Domain: Gems
Section: Cards
Category: Progression
Aliases: none.
Definition: Cards are equipable gem purchases that grant effects while slotted.
Behavior:
Cards cost 20 Gems per purchase.
Cards grant their effect only while equipped.
Cards have rarity buckets and are drawn from those buckets when purchased.
Cards can be upgraded through duplicate copies up to max level 7.

Mechanic: Card Locking
Type: Rule
Domain: Cards
Section: Cards
Category: Loadout Rules
Aliases: locked cards
Definition: Card Locking prevents equipped cards from being removed or swapped while the lock condition is active.
Behavior:
Cards with the locked icon can never be removed during the run.
When a Boss or Fleet Enemy is alive, all cards become locked until those enemies are gone.
Presets can only be swapped during a run if the locked card set stays identical.

Mechanic: Card Slots
Type: Capacity
Domain: Cards
Section: Cards
Category: Loadout Capacity
Aliases: card slots
Definition: Card Slots determine how many cards can be equipped at once.
Behavior:
Gem purchases raise card slots up to 22.
Harmony tech tree keys can raise total slots to 28.
The total Gem cost to reach 22 purchased slots is 58,400 Gems.

Mechanic: Card Slot Costs
Type: Cost Ladder
Domain: Gems
Section: Cards
Category: Loadout Capacity
Aliases: slot costs
Definition: Card Slot Costs are the Gem costs for each additional card slot.
Costs:
Slot 1 is free.
Slots 2 through 22 cost 50, 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 750, 1000, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800, 2500, 3500, 4500, 5500, 6500, 7500, 8500, and 10000 Gems.

Mechanic: Card Star Costs
Type: Copy Cost Ladder
Domain: Gems
Section: Cards
Category: Upgrade Costs
Aliases: star costs; copy costs
Definition: Card Star Costs describe how many copies and Gems are needed to raise a card through its star ladder.
Costs:
Unlocking a card costs 20 Gems for the first copy.
2-star needs 3 copies and 40 Gems.
3-star needs 5 copies and 100 Gems.
4-star needs 8 copies and 160 Gems.
5-star needs 12 copies and 240 Gems.
6-star needs 20 copies and 400 Gems.
7-star needs 32 copies and 640 Gems.
Maxing one card takes 80 copies and 1600 Gems total.
With 31 cards, maxing the full set costs 49,600 Gems.

Mechanic: Card Buying
Type: Draw System
Domain: Gems
Section: Cards
Category: Acquisition
Aliases: buy card; draw rates
Definition: Card Buying selects a rarity first and then a card within that rarity pool.
Behavior:
Base rarity chances are Common 80%, Rare 17%, and Epic 3%.
Maxed cards are removed from the draw pool.
If all Commons are maxed, Rare draw chance rises to 97%.
If all cards are maxed, the buy card button can no longer be used.
If the buy-card event mission is active after all cards are bought, it completes instantly.

Mechanic: Card Milestone Unlocks
Type: Unlock Rule
Domain: Milestones
Section: Cards
Category: Acquisition Gates
Aliases: milestone cards
Definition: Card Milestone Unlocks gate specific cards behind milestone requirements before they can enter the draw pool.
Behavior:
Recovery Package Chance unlocks at Tier 2 Wave 750.
Land Mine Stun unlocks at Tier 7 Wave 250.
Nuke unlocks at Tier 11 Wave 10.
Ultimate Crit unlocks at Tier 14 Wave 50.
Area of Effect unlocks at Tier 20 Wave 80.
If every currently available card is maxed before another milestone card unlocks, card buying stalls until the next milestone gate is cleared.
Death Ray does not have a lower draw rate than normal Epics and does not need a special unlock.

Mechanic: Card Mastery Unlock
Type: Progression Unlock
Domain: Cards
Section: Cards
Category: Masteries
Aliases: card mastery
Definition: Card Mastery Unlock enables per-card mastery upgrades once late-game card progression conditions are met.
Behavior:
Card Mastery Unlock requires 30 cards maxed and the Tier 16 Wave 100 milestone.
Each card mastery is unlocked individually on the cards page.
A mastery only applies while its card is equipped.
Unlocking a mastery costs stones and also unlocks that card's mastery labs.

